    <!-- Legal Sheets (Privacy Policy & Open Source Licenses) -->
    <string name="privacy_policy_subtitle">Data Handling &amp; Privacy Notice</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary_title">Summary</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary_body">Hello Reader is designed with privacy in mind. There are no advertising trackers, analytics SDKs, or user profiling. Network traffic flows directly between your device and your chosen Storyteller server, with third-party network access limited to optional dictionary lookups.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec1_title">1. No Developer Analytics or Tracking</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec1_body">The developers of Hello Reader do not operate analytics servers, user tracking databases, or telemetry collectors for this application. The app does not collect your name, email address, physical location, or reading activity.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec2_title">2. Network Connections &amp; Third Parties</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec2_body">• Storyteller Server: When connected, network traffic (catalog syncing, book downloads, checkpoints) is routed directly between your device and your configured server endpoint. No developer-operated proxy or relay is used.\n\n• Dictionary Lookups: When you highlight a word and select \'Define\', the word is sent via HTTPS to api.dictionaryapi.dev (Free Dictionary API) to retrieve definitions. The service receives the queried word and your IP address. No account tokens or device identifiers are sent.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec3_title">3. On-Device Storage, Tokens &amp; Backups</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec3_body">• Content &amp; Metadata: Downloaded e-books, audio files, covers, bookmarks, and reading positions are stored in private application storage on your device.\n\n• Authentication Tokens: Server authentication tokens (not passwords) are encrypted on-device via Android Keystore (EncryptedSharedPreferences) and are excluded from backups.\n\n• Android Cloud Backup: With allowBackup enabled, non-sensitive app data (such as book titles, reading checkpoints, bookmarks, and preferences) may be backed up to your personal Google account if Android Backup is enabled on your device. The encrypted credential vault is excluded from backups.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec4_title">4. Device Permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec4_body">• Camera: Used solely for scanning QR codes during server connection setup. Optical barcode scanning runs on-device via Google ML Kit, which may transmit diagnostic and usage metrics to Google as documented by Google. Camera frames are never stored or transmitted.\n\n• File Imports: The app does not request Android storage permissions. Importing books uses Android\'s system file picker, granting temporary read access only to the selected file.\n\n• Media Playback: Used solely to provide uninterrupted audiobook and narration playback in the background.\n\n• Notifications: Used solely for system lock-screen / notification shade playback controls and active download indicators.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec5_title">5. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec5_body">All local data remains under your physical control on your device. You can delete downloaded books, remove bookmarks, or disconnect server profiles at any time. Selecting \'Clear Storage\' in Android Settings or uninstalling the app permanently purges all local databases, caches, and credentials.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec6_title">6. Publisher &amp; Contact</string>
    <string name="privacy_sec6_body">For privacy questions or requests:\nchristianhokeprogramming@gmail.com\n\nCommunity (Discord):\n%1$s</string>
